# Tenacity Retry Pattern Preference
When implementing retry logic with Tenacity, use the AsyncRetrying pattern instead of decorators:

PREFERRED:
```python
from tenacity import (
    AsyncRetrying,
    before_sleep_log,
    stop_after_attempt,
    wait_exponential,
)
import logging
async for attempt in AsyncRetrying(
    stop=stop_after_attempt(5),
    wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=5, max=60),
    before_sleep=before_sleep_log(logger, logging.WARNING),
    reraise=True,
):
    with attempt:
        # your code here
```

AVOID:
```python
@retry(stop=stop_after_attempt(3), wait=wait_exponential(...))
async def my_function():
    # your code here
```

This pattern provides more explicit control over retry logic and maintains consistency with existing codebase patterns.